  "title": "Proverbs 24:23–34",
  "content": "<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\",\"contentSize\":\"720px\"},\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"padding\":{\"top\":\"2.5rem\",\"bottom\":\"4rem\"}}}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\" style=\"padding-top:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4rem\"><!-- wp:html -->\n<figure class=\"saints-chapter-emblem\" data-saints-angel-version=\"2026-09-20\"><img src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/saints-angel-bishop-150x150.png\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/saints-angel-bishop-150x150.png 150w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/09/saints-angel-bishop-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 480px) 96px, 112px\" width=\"112\" height=\"112\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"eager\"><figcaption><a class=\"saints-chapter-emblem__role\" href=\"/bible/ministry/#bishop\" title=\"The twelve ministerial roles: Bishop\">Bishop</a><span class=\"saints-chapter-emblem__separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\">·</span><span class=\"saints-chapter-emblem__meaning\">Equitable judgment</span></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1,\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#b3261e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#b3261e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontStyle\":\"normal\",\"fontWeight\":\"400\",\"fontSize\":\"2.6rem\"}}} -->\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#b3261e;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:2.6rem\">Proverbs 24:23–34</h1>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"saints-pericope\"} -->\n<p class=\"saints-pericope\">A Little Sleep, and Poverty Comes Marching</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"15px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#6b6b6b;font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/chapter-30/\">← Proverbs 30</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/\">Proverbs: all chapters</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/chapter-30-source-block-2/\">Proverbs 30:15–33 →</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"14px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#8a8a8a;font-size:14px\">Proverbs is read here in the order of the Greek text: chapters 1–24:22, then 30:1–14, 24:23–34, 30:15–33, 31:1–9, chapters 25–29, and 31:10–31.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-23\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-23\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:23</span>These things I say to you, the wise, to recognize: to show deference to a face in judgment is not good;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-24\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-24\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:24</span>One who says of the impious, “He is righteous,” will be accursed among peoples and hated among nations;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-25\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-25\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:25</span>but those who reprove will appear better, and a good blessing will come upon them;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-26\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-26\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:26</span>and lips answering good words will kiss.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-27\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-27\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:27</span>Prepare your works for going out, and make yourself ready for the field, and follow behind me, and you will rebuild your house.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-28\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-28\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:28</span>Do not be a false witness against your fellow citizen, and do not make your lips wide;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-29\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-29\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:29</span>Do not say, “As he treated me, I will treat him, and I will punish him for the wrong he did me.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-30\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-30\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:30</span>A foolish man is like a cultivated field, and a person lacking understanding like a vineyard;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-31\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-31\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:31</span>if you leave him alone, he will become wasteland, and grow wild with grass all over and become abandoned, and his stone fences are torn down.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-32\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-32\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:32</span>Afterward I reconsidered; I looked so as to choose discipline.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-33\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-33\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:33</span>“A little I doze, a little I sleep, a little I clasp my chest with my hands”—</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#3e3e3e\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"18px\"}},\"anchor\":\"v24-34\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" id=\"v24-34\" style=\"color:#3e3e3e;font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.72em;color:#8b5a2b;font-weight:600;vertical-align:super;margin-right:0.35em\">24:34</span>but if you do this, your poverty will come marching in front, and your want like a good runner.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"center\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#6b6b6b\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"15px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#6b6b6b;font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/chapter-30/\">← Proverbs 30</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/\">Proverbs: all chapters</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://staging-8e0d-waywardnightjars.wpcomstaging.com/bible/wisdom/proverbs/chapter-30-source-block-2/\">Proverbs 30:15–33 →</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"},\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"#8a8a8a\"}}},\"typography\":{\"fontSize\":\"14px\"}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-color has-link-color\" style=\"color:#8a8a8a;font-size:14px\">Bespoke Saints English Translation · 14 October 2026 · Provisional editorial edition awaiting specialist review.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<aside class=\"bespoke-current-notes\" aria-label=\"Current Bespoke editorial notes\" style=\"font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;border-top:1px solid #d4c6ad;margin-top:2rem;padding-top:1rem\"><h2>Current Bespoke editorial notes</h2><p>The newer Bespoke Saints English (1).pdf governs, with accepted Genesis 1–11 as the English benchmark. It supersedes the older Founding Style Guide where their pronoun rules conflict: Thou/Thee/Thy address God directly; ordinary address uses you/your.</p><p>Preserve both separated source blocks and additions 22a–e in their established positions. Keep steering, estate, gates, fashioned breath, seven falls, repeated word-receiving, king’s sword-tongue and bones/eaglets images. Ordinary address is singular except the plural wise audience in 23. Follow behind me and for the wrong he did me clarify 27,29 without settling the speaker identity.</p><p>Greek consultation in this revision: Publisher’s full displayed running text read in the browser for this chapter, with focused comparison of the features listed. No printed apparatus or manuscript collation. Rahlfs–Hanhart 2006 remains the user-authorized provisional base. Focused checks of the publisher’s Greek running text are recorded by chapter. This is an English editorial revision, not a complete critical-text or apparatus verification. Göttingen, full apparatus, independent Greek and human read-aloud reviews remain pending.</p><p>Further review: Review the difficult 7–10 chain, receiving/received in 22a, speaker of follow behind me in 27 and the cultivated-person comparison in 30–31. Independent Greek, Göttingen/apparatus and human read-aloud review pending.</p></aside>\n<!-- /wp:html -->\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
}
